;; expect: main.f refused bad_shape
;; a sidecar's code goes where a hole may stand and nowhere else. The entry names `n`, and the
;; only list (hole n) of this fn is a `let`'s binder — a local called `hole`, bound to n —: with
;; the code in it the list is no binder, and the fn is refused; it is never read another way.
;; Without the sidecar the file loads, its one hole `k` reported
(fn f ((n Nat)) Nat (let ((hole n)) (+ hole (hole k))))
